# Integer32 addition at the type boundary

Verifies int32 addition at the upper boundary of the 32-bit range through the
complete CLI pipeline. Every operand is int32 to keep this case focused on
same-type boundary semantics.

>>> source
left: int32 = 2147483640
right: int32 = 7
neg_left: int32 = -2147483640

// Verifies addition reaching exactly the int32 maximum.
boundary_sum: int32 = left + right
print(boundary_sum)

// Verifies addition of a negative operand staying in range.
negative_sum: int32 = neg_left + right
print(negative_sum)

<<< stdout
2147483647
-2147483633

<<< stderr
